# Line endings are pinned to LF in the index *and* the working tree.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true, which stores LF but writes CRLF on
# checkout, so every `git add` warned that the file would be rewritten and the
# working tree drifted from the index. Pinning LF makes the two agree, so a
# diff shows a content change and nothing else. Markdown, Python, JSON and
# PDFs are all read identically with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never normalised and never diffed as text.
*.pdf binary
